{"id":528,"date":"2022-09-20T10:06:42","date_gmt":"2022-09-20T00:36:42","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/feedops.com\/?p=528"},"modified":"2022-09-21T11:41:57","modified_gmt":"2022-09-21T02:11:57","slug":"map-feed-attributes","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/feedops.com\/map-feed-attributes\/","title":{"rendered":"New Feature: Feed Attribute Mapping"},"content":{"rendered":"<h1>New Feature: Website Attributes Mapping<\/h1>\n<p>FeedOps is dedicated to helping you get your product data where it needs to go.<\/p>\n<p>Today we have released a new feature that allows you to map any of your website fields to available FeedOps fields, giving you more flexibility than ever before in how you access your product data within FeedOps.<\/p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"800\" height=\"316\" src=\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/09\/image1-1024x405.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/09\/image1-1024x405.png 1024w, https:\/\/feedops.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/09\/image1-300x119.png 300w, https:\/\/feedops.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/09\/image1-768x304.png 768w, https:\/\/feedops.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/09\/image1.png 1147w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\"><\/p>\n<h2>How to map your Website Fields to FeedOps Fields<\/h2>\n<p>1: Go to Website &gt; Connect &gt; Configure Attribute Mappings<\/p>\n<p>2: Go to the Custom Field Mappings tab &gt; Add Mapping<\/p>\n<figure>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"800\" height=\"685\" src=\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/09\/image3.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/09\/image3.png 1002w, https:\/\/feedops.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/09\/image3-300x257.png 300w, https:\/\/feedops.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/09\/image3-768x658.png 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\"><figcaption><\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<p>3: Here, you can select the FeedOps field to which you want your Source field to be mapped.<\/p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"800\" height=\"508\" src=\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/09\/image2.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/09\/image2.png 988w, https:\/\/feedops.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/09\/image2-300x190.png 300w, https:\/\/feedops.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/09\/image2-768x487.png 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\"><br \/>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"800\" height=\"504\" src=\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/09\/image4.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/09\/image4.png 982w, https:\/\/feedops.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/09\/image4-300x189.png 300w, https:\/\/feedops.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/09\/image4-768x484.png 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\"><\/p>\n<p>NOTE: You also have the option to add a \u201cStatic Value\u201d. The static value applied is the one used within FeedOps for the respective field for all of your items.<\/p>\n<p>4: After applying your mappings, click the \u201cSave\u201d button.<\/p>\n<p>Please note that it might take some time (maximum a day) for your mappings to flow through in FeedOps (depending on your inventory size).<\/p>\n<h2>Other changes<\/h2>\n<p>One other minor change with this release is that you can Test\/Update your store connection details. To Test\/Update your store details go to Website &gt; Connect &gt; Edit Connection Details.<\/p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"800\" height=\"316\" src=\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/09\/image5-1024x404.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/09\/image5-1024x404.png 1024w, https:\/\/feedops.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/09\/image5-300x118.png 300w, https:\/\/feedops.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/09\/image5-768x303.png 768w, https:\/\/feedops.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/09\/image5.png 1143w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\"><br \/>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"800\" height=\"686\" src=\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/09\/image6.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/09\/image6.png 1001w, https:\/\/feedops.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/09\/image6-300x257.png 300w, https:\/\/feedops.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/09\/image6-768x658.png 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\"><\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>FeedOps helps you get your product data where it needs to be. FeedOps allows you to choose which fields from your website to use as feed attributes, giving you the flexibility to advertise the way you want.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":5,"featured_media":537,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"_acf_changed":false,"content-type":"","footnotes":""},"categories":[1],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-528","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","category-uncategorized"],"acf":[],"yoast_head":"<!-- This site is optimized with the Yoast SEO Premium plugin v26.6 (Yoast SEO v26.6) - https:\/\/yoast.com\/wordpress\/plugins\/seo\/ -->\n<title>New Feature: Feed Attribute Mapping<\/title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"FeedOps allows you to choose which fields from your website to use as feed attributes, giving you the flexibility to advertise the way you want.\" \/>\n<meta name=\"robots\" content=\"index, follow, max-snippet:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-video-preview:-1\" \/>\n<link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https:\/\/feedops.com\/map-feed-attributes\/\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en